	(text "5.1k on CC1 and CC2 tells a USB-C source we are a 5 V device. U4 clamps ESD on D+, D- and VBUS.\nD1 and Q1 join the two 5 V sources: Q1 passes CN105 5 V with ~30 mV drop and is switched off by USB 5 V, so neither source back-feeds the other."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 38.1 127 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0ab1a9a1-8b89-4f88-886f-755e6f3dc9e0")
	)
	(text "CN105 (JST PA, 2.0 mm): 1 = 12 V (unused)   2 = GND   3 = 5 V   4 = TX from heat pump (5 V)   5 = RX into heat pump\nVerify this pinout on YOUR unit with a meter before plugging anything in.\nD3 clamps the 5 V pin at ~9 V if a cable ever puts 12 V on it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 38.1 50.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0fa2208b-b001-4d54-8e18-a2dca1192235")
	)
	(text "R2/R3 divide 5 V down to 3.0 V\nfor the ESP32-C6 RX pin (max 3.6 V)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 38.1 101.6 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "145b197b-cefc-4483-aa42-574f5f90128e")
	)
	(text "USB-C (programming + bench power)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 38.1 121.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "30abe81c-d121-4f46-a529-ba6c5a3bdc24")
	)
	(text "UART1 on IO6/IO7 talks to the heat pump.\nIO4, IO5, IO8, IO9, IO15 are boot-strapping pins: IO9 (BOOT button) and IO8 each get a 10k pull-up (R12, R11) so boot mode is never left to the weak internal pull-ups. IO12/IO13 are the native USB pins."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 247.65 50.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "3826f926-a027-4721-a613-1de421e3b65d")
	)
	(text "3.3 V REGULATOR"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 162.56 198.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "4a931565-960e-4f6e-a0f0-373f1ac2c6b9")
	)
	(text "U3 is powered from 5 V: 3.3 V in -> 5 V out\nso the heat pump sees clean 5 V logic.\n~OE tied low = always enabled.\nR6 keeps TX idle-high while the ESP boots."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 88.9 101.6 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6e9ebbc2-cc09-4afd-ab19-f756788f19a8")
	)
	(text "C7: bulk reservoir for Wi-Fi TX bursts\nwhen fed from the heat pump. Place near Q1."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 136.525 85.09 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a4f609f7-c155-4fae-96fa-c6c04aeb7fcc")
	)
	(text "AP2112K-3.3: 600 mA, 0.25 V dropout. Wi-Fi TX bursts are the worst case.\nPWR_FLAGs tell ERC that +5V, 5V_USB, 5V_CN105 and GND are really powered."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 162.56 203.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "afa8848b-c8ac-4875-9f8a-5c6a4bee8e8f")
	)
	(text "ESP32-C6 MODULE"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 247.65 45.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b2744d2d-1f36-4f5e-bb7b-0b12f1192367")
	)
	(text "CN105 INTERFACE"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 38.1 44.196 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c69f4578-7f87-46b5-91a4-699e40ef5069")
	)
